ivider, bottom row: \"© 2020 Foodieland. All rights reserved.\" centered, social icons right. Dark or light? Brand tint? I'll do white footer with light divider — consistent light mode. Text dark.\n\nNewsletter card component: 1280 x 442, brand tint background #E7F9FD, radius 24? Original: light blue bg, radius ~30? Title 48 semibold centered \"Deliciousness to your inbox\", copy centered, email field + Subscribe button centered, decorations: vegetables bottom-left, salad bottom-right, leaf. \n\nRecipe card component: white card 290x316 with photo (rounded 20? inner image), title 18 semibold (2 lines), meta row (timer 30 Minutes, fork category), favorite button top-right over photo (white circle 48 with heart; favorited = red heart). Photo inside card: I'll place the photo instance inside card with rounded corners via clipsContent frame. Component must accept different photos per instance — override photo by swapping? Can't swap images inside instance easily... I can override the instance's fills or resize... Better: make Recipe Card NOT include photo as nested fixed; instead make card component with a placeholder photo area (a frame named \"Photo\") and per-instance I can override the photo's source? Instances can't swap child for different component without exposed props... In plugin API, `swapComponent` on nested instances inside an instance is NOT allowed (read-only structure). Hmm.\n\nOptions: (a) Don't make recipe card a component with photo inside; make \"Recipe Card\" a component that includes a default photo instance, and for each usage create instance then DETACH? Detaching loses component reuse credit.\n\n(b) Use variant property approach: make Recipe Card a variant set with 16 photo variants — too many.\n\n(c) Override image fill: The photo components (e.g., 7:31 Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice) are components with image fills. Inside my card instance, I can find the nested photo instance and... can't swap. BUT I can instead place in the card a plain rectangle