{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":45253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"08196ae79a270a7ade7d1911310f6cfd","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Primitive components done. Now build bigger components: Header, Footer, Newsletter Card, Recipe Card, Promo Card, Instagram Post, Author/Meta pieces, Ingredient Item, Direction Step, Nutrition Panel, Article Item, Tasty Recipe Item, Pagination, Select Field, Textarea.\n\nNote: components with layout — I'll continue building in the same Components frame.\n\nLet me carefully build:\n\n**Recipe Card** (288w, VERTICAL):\n- Photo wrapper frame (240w... wait I said card 288: photo 240? Let me set card width 288, photo fill width 240h, radius 20; padding 16. So photo = 288-32=256w? No: card padding 16, photo width 288-32=256, height 190? Hmm original design: cards 290w x 316h with image 250x180. I'll do: card 288w, padding 16, photo 256×180, gap 16, title 18 SemiBold lh140 (auto-height, stretch width), meta row H gap 24: chip time + chip category.\n- Favorite absolute at photo top-right: 16px inset → x = 288-16-48-16? The wrapper approach: card as frame with padding; favorite positioned absolute on photo. With auto-layout, absolute-positioning children is allowed (`child.layoutPositioning = 'ABSOLUTE'`). Yes! Figma supports absolute position within auto-layout frames. I'll use that: fav absolute at right=16+16... Actually constraints: with absolute positioning, set x,y manually after; constraints may keep them. Simplest: after appending, set fav.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE', then fav.x = cardW-16-48, fav.y=16. Constraint default top-left — fine for fixed size.\n\nFor instance photos: each recipe card instance gets its photo instance with fixed size 256×180.\n\n**Promo Card** (400×434): VERTICAL center, padding 32, gap 24: Title text 'Don't forget to eat healthy food' 24 SemiBold center lh130; Photo_Ad_Salad instance 232×220; URL 'www.foodieland.com' 16 Medium alpha60 center.\n\n**Newsletter Card** (1280×440): relative frame, TINT bg, radius 32, clips. Center content (VERTICAL, align center, gap 24): Title 48 SemiBold 'Deliciousness to your inbox'; copy 16 Regular alpha60 lh160 center, width 620: 'Get new recipes and cooking tips in your inbox every week. No spam, unsubscribe anytime.'; form row H gap 16: field (white bg, radius 16, 380×64, placeholder text 'Your email address...' 15 Regular alpha50, left padding 20) + Button md? Button with h64: use Button / lg instance (60h) — make field 380×60 then. Center row vertically.\nDecors absolute: Vegetables bottom-left (scale ~1.6 → 197×192 at x~ -20, y bottom), Salad bottom-right (~160), Leaf top-right small rotated. With clipsContent true on card. Since content uses auto layout with absolute decors — decors must be absolute children too.\n\n**Header** (1440×96): HORIZONTAL, padding L/R 64, align CENTER, justify SPACE_BETWEEN: left logo (Logo_Foodieland 110×19), nav row (H gap 8: nav item instances ×5), right social group. Nav instances: I'll create instances inside component (one Default ×4, one Current) and swap text per instance later.\n\n**Footer** (1440×~150): \n- Frame HORIZONTAL padding 64, pt 32, justify SPACE_BETWEEN: left: logo + tagline 'Simple, tasty recipes for every day.' (16 alpha60) — vertical gap 8; center: links row 'Recipes Blog Contact About us' gap 40 16 Medium; right: social group. Then divider bottom + copyright: simpler: footer = VERTICAL: row1 space-between as above; row2: divider line (1280×1 alpha 10) + copyright text centered? Data: '© 2020 Foodieland. All rights reserved.' Put divider then copyright centered with padding.\n\n**Instagram Post** (290w, white, radius 16, shadow): VERTICAL:\n- header row (H gap 10, pl 12 pr 12 pt 12 pb 10, align center): avatar 28 round; col: 'Foodieland.' 13 SemiBold lh130, 'Tokyo, Japan' 11 alpha50; spacer; Icon_More.\n- photo 290×200 (stretch).\n- counter chip: absolute top-right of photo: '1/3' 11 Medium white on black60 round 10.\n- actions row (H pl12 pr12 pt10 gap 16, align center): like, comment, send; spacer; save.\n- liked text (pl12 pr12): 'Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others' 12 SemiBold.\n- caption (pl12 pr12 pt4): caption 12 Regular lh150.\n- date (pl12 pr12 pt6 pb14): 'September 19' 11 alpha40 uppercase? keep normal.\nHeights: 12+28+10 + 200 + ... ≈ 340.\n\n**Recipe Meta** (for hero, small): H gap 16: avatar 40; col: name 16 Bold, date 14 Medium alpha60.\n\n**Ingredient Item**: H gap 16 pt 16 pb 16 align center, stretch width; checkbox circle 24 (white border black10; checked: black fill + white check icon); label 18 Regular. Divider bottom: use strokes: item strokes bottom 1px black10.\n\n**Direction Step**: VERTICAL gap 16 stretch; header row H gap 24 align center: big number '1' 24 SemiBold in circle? Original has numbered circle with serif? Keep: circle 40 black tint bg with number 16 SemiBold, title 24 SemiBold lh130; then body 16 Regular alpha60 lh160. Checkbox for step: brief says \"3 steps, each with checkbox, number, title and text\". So each step row: checkbox circle + number+title. I'll put checkbox at left of number? Let me structure: header row: [NumberBadge (1,2,3)] [Title] ... and checkbox? Hmm \"each with checkbox, number, title and text\". So each step: checkbox (round, like ingredients), number, title, text. Header row: checkbox 24, number text '1.' 24 SemiBold, title 24 SemiBold. Body indented under title.\nI'll do: H gap 20 align center: checkbox, then text runs: number+title combined? Keep separate: number '1' 24 Bold, title 20 SemiBold. Body below padding-left 44.\n\n**Nutrition Panel**: TINT bg radius 24, VERTICAL padding 32 gap 24, width 400: Title 'Nutrition Information' 24 SemiBold; rows (5): each H space-between pt 14 pb 14 border-bottom 1 black10: label 18 Medium alpha60, value 18 Medium; note text 14 Regular alpha50 lh160.\n\n**Article Item** (row, 760w): H gap 24 pt/pb 24, align center: photo 220×150 radius 16; col VERTICAL gap 10 stretch: title 20 SemiBold lh140; excerpt 14 Regular alpha60 lh160 (2 lines); author row: avatar 32 + name 14 SemiBold + dot + date 14 Medium alpha50.\n\n**Tasty Recipe Item** (row): H gap 20 align center: photo 120×90 radius 12; col: title 16 SemiBold lh140; 'By Andreas Paula' 13 Medium alpha50.\n\n**Pagination**: H gap 12: page buttons 40×40 radius 12: current black bg white text; others tint bg. Items: 1,2,3,4,5,…, chevron-right button.\n\n**Select Field**: like Text Field: label + input with value text + chevron down icon right.\n\n**Textarea Field**: label + input 160h with placeholder.\n\n**Search Bar**: field 460×60 with placeholder + Button md 'Search'.\n\nAlso **Author Meta** inline component? For recipe meta row (02): vertical stack PREP TIME/COOK TIME etc. Just build inline in frame.\n\nLet me also decide grid: content width 1280 (64px margins). 4-col card grid: card 288 × gap 32: 288*4+32*3 = 1152+96=1248. Hmm 1280-1248=32 → margins 96? Let me recompute: 1280 width content; 4 cards + 3 gaps = 1280 → gap=(1280-1152)/3=42.67. Ugly. Use card 296: 296*4=1184, gap=(1280-1184)/3=32. \n\nCategories: 6 tiles 180w + gaps: 180*6=1080, gap 40 → 1080+200=1280. tile 180 wide. Adjust Category Tile to 180? The tile component I made is 148w; instance can resize to 180 (stretch image? image fixed 110 center). It's fine: set instance width 180 — auto-layout stretch? counterAxis sizing FIXED in component (fixed 148). Resizing instance width to 180 works (component frame resize allowed on instance). Image stays 110 centered. OK.\n\nRecipe card: change to 296 width? Component currently... I haven't made Recipe Card yet. I'll make it 296w with photo 264×180 (padding 16).\n\nHome layout plan:\n- Header 1440×96\n- Hero 1280: H gap 40: left col ~ (build in auto layout) \n  Actually hero: single frame 1280×~660, relative: left content padding 48: badge chip (Icon_Hot_Recipes + 'Hot Recipes'), title 56 SemiBold? Use 52. copy, meta row, CTA row; right photo 620×620? total height ~ 640.\n  Badge: chip with Icon_Hot_Recipes image 24×24 + 'Hot Recipes'.\n  Title: 'Spicy delicious chicken wings' 52 SemiBold lh120 → 2 lines at ~480w.\n  Copy: featured copy 16 Regular alpha60 lh160.\n  Chips row: Chip(30 Minutes) + Chip(Chicken w/ fork knife).\n  Meta: avatar 40 + John Smith / 15 March 2022.\n  CTA: Button lg with text 'View Recipes' + Icon_Play white right? Button / lg instance, set label 'View Recipes', append? Instance label is auto-layout hug... Adding icon to instance is impossible (can't add children to instances). So CTA = custom row: Button / lg instance + separate play circle? Brief: \"View Recipes\" (Icon_Play) — button with play icon inside. Since I can't add children into an instance, options: build CTA as a one-off group (not instance) replicating button style with icon; or wrap: absolute-position a play icon over the button instance right side. Simpler: CTA button as standalone structure (black rounded rect 200×60, label + play icon white 20). It's a one-off — acceptable, still visually consistent. Actually — better: make a component variant 'Button / lg with icon'? I can create another component 'Button / icon' with label+icon. Then per instance swap icon? The icon inside instance — swap requires nested instance replace: instance.swapComponent works on nested instances! So 'Button / icon' component contains an instance of Icon_Play? No wait — swapping the icon instance within a button instance: nested instance swapping is allowed (it's an override). OK but I only need one such button; just build it inline in hero. Fine.\n\n- Categories section: header row (title left 40 SemiBold 'Categories', Button md 'View All Categories' right) + row of 6 tiles.\n- Simple and tasty: header center: title 'Simple and tasty recipes' 40, copy center 16 alpha60 (maxwidth 700). Grid 4×2 of recipe cards (with promo card replacing 6th position): order: 1 burger, 2 salmon, 3 pancake, 4 salad, 5 meatballs, [promo], 6 fruity pancake, 7 one pot, 8 pasta. So grid positions: 8 cards + promo in middle (row2 col2?). Original Foodieland: promo is 6th (row 2, position 2). I'll place: row1: cards 1-4; row2: card5, promo, card6, card7; row3: card8? That breaks 4-col. Original: grid 3 rows? No — original home \"Simple recipes\" has 9 items in 3-col? The original kit: \"Simple and tasty recipes\" grid 4 cols x 2 rows with ad at position 6 (row2 col2), meaning only 7 cards + ad. But we have 8 cards + ad = 9 items → 4+4+1? Awkward. Alternative: 3 cols × 3 rows: row1: c1 c2 c3; row2: c4 AD c5; row3: c6 c7 c8. That's 3 cols of 400w cards. Card 400w: 400*3+40*2=1280. Nice: gap 40. Cards bigger: photo 368×220.\n  Let me make Recipe Card 400w variant? A single card component resized: card instances resize to 400 wide (photo instance stretches if photo wrapper is stretch... photo is instance fixed size; in auto-layout, set photo instance layoutAlign STRETCH in component so when card resizes, photo stretches? Instances: resizing child instances via layoutAlign STRETCH works within auto-layout (fill). Set photo img fill scaleMode FILL (it's FILL already) so crop adapts. \n  So Recipe Card component: width 400 (VERTICAL, padding 16, gap 16): photo instance layoutAlign STRETCH height 220 fixed... in auto-layout, child with layoutAlign STRETCH fills counter axis; main-axis size fixed? For VERTICAL container, counter axis = horizontal → stretch width; height fixed 220. But instance height fixed — resize card width → photo stretches. \n  For More recipes section: 4 cols × 2 rows of smaller cards: width 296: resize instances to 296; photo stretches to 264 wide, height stays 220 → ratio fine.\n  \n  So one Recipe Card component reused at 400 and 296 widths. Title sizes: default 20 SemiBold? At 400: title 24? Keep 20 for all, lh 140. Meta chips inside.\n\n- Chef promo: H gap 64: left col: title 'Everyone can be a che