/ lg instance? can't append. Build ad hoc \"Hero Button\" — fine (reuse visually). Actually to satisfy \"reuse\", most buttons are instances; hero has icon so ad hoc acceptable. Or place play icon beside button? Ad hoc better visually.\n   - Hero background: subtle tint gradient? Keep white; left column maybe tint pill only.\n   Hero total height: padding 80 + 640 = 800. Left column vertically centered: wrap hero H AL align CENTER.\n3. Categories (1440, V AL pt 80 pb 40 pl/pr 80, gap 40): header row (title 36 \"Categories\" + right \"View All Categories\" tint pill button (ad hoc: tint bg, semibold 16, radius 16, h 44)) ; tiles row gap 32: 6 category tile instances with images/labels swapped.\n4. Simple and tasty (pt 40 pb 40 pl/pr 80 gap 48): section head (title center? original centers titles with copy under). Brief: \"Simple and tasty recipes\" + copy. I'll center: V AL align CENTER gap 16: title 40 Bold centered; copy 16 centered w 640; then grid: two rows of 4 recipe cards (H AL gap 24): 8 cards. Row structure: V AL gap 24 with two H rows. Plus promo card? Promo belongs to \"Simple and tasty recipes\" per brief (\"8 recipe cards ... promo card\"). Grid 4 cols × 2 rows = 8 slots but we have 8 cards + promo. Make 3 rows? Better: last row = 3 cards + promo (9 slots total)? That breaks order. Alternative layout: 2 rows × 4 = 8 cards; promo card floats right of title? Hmm.\n   Decision: \"Simple and tasty\" section grid: row1: cards 1-4, row2: cards 5-8. Promo card displayed in \"More recipes\"? No — brief assigns promo to Simple and tasty section on 01. But \"More recipes\" also has 8 cards; promo could fit naturally as 9th slot there... yet brief explicitly lists promo under Simple and tasty. Keep promo in Simple-and-tasty: grid 3×3? cols: (1280 - 2*24)/3 = 410 cards? Cards are 290.\n   Option: row1: 4 cards; row2: 4 cards; row3: promo + 2 cards? No.\n   Option: make Simple-and-tasty grid 4 cols; cards 1-8 occupy slots 1-8; promo occupies... add row3 with promo spanning? Awkward.\n   Alternative: promo card (290) as part of a 9-cell grid where grid is 4 cols: row1: 1,2,3,4; row2: 5,6,7,8; then promo centered alone? Or promo card width 290 same as card, placed in row 2 as slot 5: row2: promo,5,6,7? Then card 8 in row3 alone? Ugly.\n   Better: put promo into the More recipes grid (4×2 + promo? same issue).\n   Practical approach used by original Foodieland: the promo appears inside \"Simple and tasty\" grid as one of the 6? In original Foodieland home: \"Simple and tasty recipes\" grid has 6 slots: 5 cards + 1 ad card (the salad). Here we have 8 cards + promo. I'll do 3 rows: row1 cards 1–4, row2 cards 5–8, row3: promo card + 2 cards? There are no more cards.\n   OK compromise: grid 4 cols; rows: [1,2,3,4], [5,6,7,8], [promo + decorative copy]? no.\n   Hmm — actually could make Simple-and-tasty 5 columns? 1280/5 → 232 cards too small.\n   Let me reconsider: On 02/04/05 the promo card is in sidebar next to \"Other Recipe\"/\"Tasty Recipes\". On 01 it must appear in Simple-and-tasty. I'll make the section asymmetric: left = 8 cards in 2 rows of 4? and promo on right of section header row (next to title/copy). Layout: header row: left title+copy, right promo card? Title centered though.\n   Final decision: Section V AL: centered title + copy; then H AL (gap 24): grid (V of 2 H rows, 4 cards each = 8) width 4*290+3*24=1232... plus promo 290 → total 1546 > 1280. No.\n   Alternative: cards row of 3 per row: 3 rows: [1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,promo]. Width 3*290+2*24=918 — leaves whitespace on 1440. Could use bigger cards 400 wide: 3*400+2*32=1264. Card component resize: instance resize(400, ...) — internal image is absolute 266×180 → won't scale. Recipe card inner photo is absolute in imgWrap — instance resize stretches? Non-AL children don't stretch. The Recipe Card imgWrap child is absolute (frame with abs photo+fav). Resizing instance would distort? Frame children keep position; imgWrap is AL child with hug... imgWrap itself is absolut