stances where practical and frames elsewhere is fine.\n\nOption B: Build the Recipe Card component WITHOUT a photo, and overlay/insert photo as sibling? The photo sits inside 'Image' wrap frame in the master. If instead the master card's Image area is a plain rectangle placeholder and instances get an image instance placed as absolute child of the card instance... appending new children to an instance is also not allowed? Actually you CAN append children to an instance? No — instances can't have children appended either. Structure is fixed.\n\nOption C: Keep photos as separate absolutely-positioned nodes ON TOP of card instances (i.e., card instance with a hole). Ugly and fragile.\n\nOption D: Use multiple masters: one Recipe Card master per photo? 20 cards with unique photos — could create variants programmatically: clone the master for each photo. That gives \"instances\" of per-recipe components. Honestly simplest robust approach: build cards as plain frames via a helper function (same visual design), and ALSO keep master components in the library (Recipe Card etc. used where no swap needed, e.g., recommended cards? they also need photo swaps...).\n\nActually wait — there IS a supported way: instance.swap... no, that's for swapping whole instances. But what about `instance.exposedInstances`? No.\n\nAlternative supported pattern: **detach instance** — `instance.detachInstance()` converts to frame, then I can modify freely. Detached cards are still visually identical; reuse is arguable but the design system showcase exists. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: Figma DOES allow editing instance children in many ways: fills, text, visibility, resizing, swapping nested instances via swapInstance? There's `InstanceNode.swapInstance(component)`? No... Actually there IS: nested instance swapping is a real Figma feature (instance swap in UI). Plugin API: `instanceNode.mainComponent` can be reassigned on nested instances! Yes — for a nested instance inside an instance, you